  "step_2": "The individual describes considering the sums (outcomes) and their associated probabilities. They first mention using expected value as a criterion ('die lotterie die die höhere erwartete auszahlung hat'), but then note that the expected values are equal (both lotteries have an expected value of 0 Euros). After this, they state a preference rule: 'besser nichts als chance auf verlust' ('better nothing than a chance of loss'), which indicates a preference for avoiding any risk of loss, even if the expected value is the same. This suggests the individual chose Lottery A because it guarantees no loss, unlike Lottery B, which involves a 50% chance of losing 6000 Euros. The justification is thus based on loss avoidance and certainty, not on comparing probabilities of maximum outcomes.",
